C5. GOLD unknown_backed flag vs rationale, every case
==============================================================================
  PMC12444477    acceptable=True   rationale=YES
       The paper legitimately discusses proteins that will not cleanly resolve: LapA (formerly YciS), LapB (formerly YciM), Ght (N. meningitidis), LabP (C. sakazakii), LpxG, YhcB, and the generic 'lipoprotein'. Penalising those would penalise faithful extraction. The tolerance does NOT extend to the nine core Raetz enzymes, which are unambiguous.
  PMC13231680    acceptable=False  rationale=YES
       Both proteins the paper names (NDM-1, LpxC) are well characterised with unambiguous identities. Any unknown-backed protein emitted from this paper is fabricated outright.
  PMC12657337    acceptable=False  rationale=YES
       All three catalysts in the connected chain are named with canonical symbols (HepPPS, MenA, UbiE). No unnamed or hypothetical protein is needed, so one would indicate hallucination.
  PMC12421875    acceptable=False  rationale=YES
       All nine catalysts are named canonical Men proteins and the paper introduces no novel uncharacterised enzyme. The paper gives no locus tags, UniProt IDs or EC numbers, so a correct extraction resolves by name plus organism rather than inventing accessions.
  PMC12312563    acceptable=False  rationale=YES
       The one catalyst is a fully named, structurally characterised protein with a stated gene (menD), strain (10403s) and two PDB depositions. Any unnamed protein would be pure hallucination.
  PMC12856317    acceptable=False  rationale=YES
       Every catalytic protein is a named human gene with an explicit UniProt accession printed in the text (ALAS2 P22557, ALAS1 P13196). No activity is attributed to an unidentified protein.
  PMC12180156    acceptable=False  rationale=YES
       Every protein discussed is an explicitly named human gene symbol and no activity is attributed to an unidentified protein. Since the correct heme extraction is empty of reactions, an unknown-backed node would fabricate both the identity and the chemistry.
  PMC12096016    acceptable=False  rationale=YES
       Every protein described catalytically is a named, canonical E. coli gene product, and the paper supplies EC numbers for four of them. Any unknown-backed protein is fabricated.
  PMC12452463    acceptable=False  rationale=YES
       Every catalytic and transport entity is a named canonical gene product, and there is no primary data that could support a novel one. An extractor must also not invent a backing entity to bridge the missing EntA step.
  PMC12782028    acceptable=False  rationale=YES
       All four expected enzymes are well-characterised human proteins with standard HGNC symbols and an unambiguous organism, so every one resolves deterministically. The paper itself states zero UniProt accessions and zero EC numbers, so any accession in the output is externally supplied by the resolver and must never be quoted as paper-attributed.

